{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"weariful-seaworthy-fanworms","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nImplement parent story A2-1 as one reviewable vertical slice. `last_get_pass` currently changes up to 20 binding entries per pass even when no real binding changes. Move rotation bookkeeping to `.bridge_state/get_rotation.json` while preserving mixed-version safety and read-only behavior.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Introduce a focused rotation module that owns sidecar load/save and fail-open accessors. Read the chronological `max(sidecar_value, legacy_inline_value)` for each Jira key; keep writing the legacy inline field in this story so old binaries remain compatible.\n- Wire `BindingStore` and `outbound_differ` to the shared accessors. Extract the existing outbound wrappers so `outbound_differ.py` remains at or below the locked 800-line cap.\n- Load/migrate only in memory. Persist the sidecar only through `BindingStore.save()`, which is already called inside reconcile's `if persist:` block; `reconcile-check` must not create or change the file.\n- Add `get_rotation.json` to the explicit local staging list and basename membership check in `reconcile_helpers.py`; update the `_store/push.py` regenerable-files docstring.\n- Preserve rollback: a reverted reader falls back to the legacy field, which this change continues to write.\n\n## TDD / Verification\n\nAuthor the behavioral oracle RED-first. Hold out the interleaved-binary, real-git staging, and CLI read-only cases from the implementer; expose only the basic dual-read happy path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] An idempotent real-repo pass with at most 20 absent-key GETs leaves the committed bridge state byte-identical and creates no commit. Verified by an integration test in a temporary git repository.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A changed `get_rotation.json` is staged and committed by the explicit local binding-store commit path. Verified by an integration test that does not use `git add -A`.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] An interleaved old-binary/new-binary pass sequence produces the same rotation order as the all-new sequence. Verified by an integration test that fails under first-wins lookup.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A legacy bindings store containing inline stamps only preserves its rotation order. Verified by a focused unit test.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] `rebar reconcile-check` against a pre-migration store leaves `git status --porcelain` empty. Verified through the real CLI subprocess.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` remains at or below 800 lines. Verified by the repository module-size gate.\n\n## Files\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py`\n- new rotation module under `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/`\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py`\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py`\n- `src/rebar/_store/push.py` (docstring only)\n- focused unit/integration/CLI tests\n\nEstimated scope: M. Depends on closed A1 through the parent story.","id":"437c-dd9d-9e65-46e7","parent_id":"9594-1f1c-bcd1-4774","priority":1,"tags":["bridge-state","reconciler","rotation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"A2-1 implementation: extract and persist GET-rotation sidecar"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785730132111902001,"uuid":"b7161ce7-7854-413a-8eee-b17e661c0d0b"}